comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T13:21:04.596Z","harness:codex","Scope decision: this bundle will publish reusable intent and budget contract primitives and fix discovery costs, but it will not yet alter get/list/context/next field projections; returning the read-projection feature to open so its byte-stability acceptance is not overstated."
  "2026-07-28T15:07:12.789Z","harness:claude-code","Cost of the mandated orientation sequence, measured 2026-07-28 on the live 2,172-item tracker. The four commands AGENTS.md requires before creating work cost 16,631 bytes in default TOON output: context --limit 10 is 7,517, search with a ten-row limit 3,980, list-open --limit 20 4,759, list-in-progress --limit 20 375. Adding next --limit 5 at 8,901 brings the preamble an agent pays before touching any work to 25,532 bytes, about 6,400 tokens. next is the single largest contributor at 35 percent of the total, consistent with the earlier finding that it spends 47 percent of its own payload on the blocked companion. Encoding delta measured on the same call: context --limit 10 --json is 10,277 bytes against 7,517 for TOON, 37 percent more. This is the number that justifies this item existing: an intent projection that answers what should I do next about X in one call is competing against a 25 kB four-call preamble, not against a single cheap read. Cross-referenced on pm-5t33or as an output-cost datapoint and on pm-n7rr as a simplification lever."
  "2026-07-29T16:55:47.296Z","harness:claude-code","Orientation cost re-measured at build 2026.7.29 on the real 2,193-item tracker.\n\nThe four commands the repository's own agent guidance mandates before creating work now total 17,840 bytes, about 4,460 tokens: context --limit 10 at 8,178 B, search with a keyword --limit 10 at 4,089 B, list-open --limit 20 at 5,086 B, list-in-progress --limit 20 at 487 B. The same preamble measured 25,532 bytes, about 6,383 tokens, on 2026-07-28. That is a 30 percent reduction in one day, attributable to the lean mutation envelopes and omission receipts that landed in the 2026-07-29 lanes rather than to any change in this item's scope.\n\nAdjacent per-command costs measured in the same run, for the intent-projection design: next --limit 5 8,651 B, get pm-doxj --depth brief 4,027 B, stats 440 B, validate --json 108,652 B, validate plain 22,479 B.\n\nTwo points this sharpens for the --for projection design. First, the preamble is now dominated by context and next, which overlap heavily in content - both assemble an active working set, and an agent that runs both pays twice for one answer. Second, stats at 440 bytes proves an orientation answer can be delivered in three figures of bytes; the gap between 440 and 4,460 is the space a declared intent should be able to close.\n"
  "2026-07-29T21:56:40.194Z","harness:codex","Tranche boundary after implementation design review: this delivery does not add a partial --for flag. A complete intent contract needs a registry, exact field groups per surface, workspace and package contributions, canonical suggestions, token-budget composition, and measured deltas. The current branch only inspected this item while implementing the prerequisite generic projection declaration. Releasing it open unchanged for a cohesive future lane."
  "2026-07-30T06:47:36.454Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: CLI, SDK, and MCP now share six built-in intent projections; explicit caller flags win over defaults; direct SDK runAction next --for execute was verified from an isolated packed-package install with ready_only=true and token_budget=1200."
  "2026-07-30T07:18:54.909Z","harness:codex","Tranche boundary: this PR lands the typed built-in intent registry, CLI/SDK/MCP --for execution, nearest-match guidance, explicit-override composition, discovery, and token-budget-safe defaults. Remaining acceptance is runtime loading of workspace/package declarations, per-result-size token delta publication, and a combined relevance-plus-budget proof; returning the canonical feature open rather than overstating completion."
  "2026-07-30T07:40:02.793Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/822 carries the cohesive SDK/CLI self-describing context-contract bundle. Initial implementation commit e1fabaa97; final exact-head checks and review evidence will be recorded in the PR because post-review tracker mutations would create a new unreviewed Git tree."
  "2026-07-30T07:50:35.290Z","harness:codex","Greptile P1 review correction on PR #822: list --for triage previously selected brief despite declaring governance, ownership, and dependency groups. It now selects the exact bounded field set for those groups; explicit projection overrides still win and focused CLI/SDK intent tests pass."
  "2026-07-30T08:15:43.824Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence for PR #822 review-fix head: sandboxed repository coverage passed 403 files / 6,555 tests at exact 100% statements (46,165/46,165), branches (33,054/33,054), functions (9,430/9,430), and lines (44,824/44,824). Packed unrelated-directory acceptance verified contained executable resolution, stdin-backed create description, CLI triage intent projection, SDK six-intent and 201-code catalogs, npx, and bunx at version 2026.7.30."
  "2026-07-30T11:24:19.441Z","harness:codex","Tranche evidence: all six built-in intents now execute through CLI and SDK with valid command mappings, bounded receipts, and canonical usage errors; row metadata composes at shared egress. This parent remains open for workspace/package-declared intents and published per-result token deltas."
  "2026-07-30T11:31:00.406Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/829 reviews cohesive SDK context budgets, universal row contracts, bounded graph/health diagnostics, quality ratchets, and exact-head commit e53544cd1."
  "2026-07-30T11:54:26.980Z","harness:codex","Evidence clarification: e53544cd1 identifies the implementation commit. Exact-head review and merge proof is maintained on PR #829 because every append-only PM evidence mutation necessarily creates a newer Git head."
  "2026-07-30T17:15:07.160Z","harness:claude-code","Intent-namespace half verified 2026-07-30 (evening) at HEAD. The unreachable-intent defect this feature carried is closed correctly and I re-measured the exact reproduction. Both context intents now resolve by name, and an undeclared intent produces one structured envelope with a stable error code, an exit code of 2, and a suggestion, instead of the previous pair of contradictory validators that returned two different exit codes and advice naming a flag that was never passed. The projection half works on the three commands that had no projection at all: list, get and search now render the declared field groups and their receipts sit inside their declared ceilings.\n\nThe residual is not in the namespace, it is in the numbers, and it is now tracked as a separate issue parented under the output-budget contract. Three of the five intents this feature declares cannot emit any result on this tracker because their declared ceiling is below the smallest projection their command can render. next execute measures a 1,438-token floor against a declared 1200, context orient 8,417 against 2400, context handoff the same shape. The same five intents all fit on a two-item workspace, so the declarations were calibrated at a scale the product does not target. This falsifies the part of this feature's own promise that says an agent gets the declared field groups: on the two orientation intents an agent gets an omission receipt and a suggestion to re-run the unprojected command, which emits 12,879 bytes against the 400-byte receipt it replaces.\n\nNothing here argues for reverting the intent layer. The projection mechanism is right and the enforcement point is right. The declarations need to be functions of the corpus rather than constants, which is recorded as the roadmap horizon this pass added."
  "2026-08-01T21:15:41.935Z","harness:codex","Tranche boundary 2026-08-01: this branch consumes the shipped intent projections in the composite token-accounting acceptance corpus, but does not implement runtime workspace/package declaration loading. Releasing the claim and returning the item to open so only actively edited work remains in progress."
  "2026-08-02T17:24:13.546Z","harness:codex","Evidence 2026-08-02: request-scoped workspace and active-package intent declarations now compose before dispatch and are isolated across concurrent SDK calls. Measured on the live 2,278-item repository with JSON token accounting and no extensions: context:orient 3,214 to 2,614 estimated tokens (-600, 18.7%); context:handoff 3,200 to 1,654 (-1,546, 48.3%); get:inspect 2,851 to 2,946 (+95, -3.4% because the intent preserves lifecycle context and adds its receipt); list:triage 18,829 to 4,129 (-14,700, 78.1%); next:execute 3,540 to 1,632 (-1,908, 53.9%); search:discover 5,472 to 2,478 (-2,994, 54.7%). The positive reductions and the truthful get expansion are retained as per-intent evidence rather than hiding a non-reduction."
  "2026-08-02T18:17:08.817Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence 2026-08-02: implemented request-scoped workspace and active-package intent declarations at .agents/pm/context-intents.json and package contextIntents/context_intents exports; AsyncLocal isolation prevents concurrent SDK calls from leaking declarations; canonical nearest-match validation, relevance composition, cost budgeting, explicit-override precedence, and unchanged legacy projections are covered. Linked PM suites passed 26, 34, 46, and 135 tests. Full repository coverage passed 421 files / 6,730 tests at exact 100% statements (47,814/47,814), branches (34,517/34,517), functions (9,762/9,762), and lines (46,377/46,377). Strict lint passed with zero ESLint findings, zero jscpd clones across 864 files, zero static-quality violations, and 100% source/export/member docstrings. Unrelated packed npm and Bun consumers resolved only their local tarball binary; direct CLI, npx --no-install, Bun binary, bunx --bun, SDK imports, workspace intent discovery, canonical override precedence, bounded omission receipts, and mutation rejection all passed. Telemetry flushed the acceptance actions in real time with zero invalid rows and no failed flush; Sentry reports zero unresolved issues seen in the last 24 hours."
  "2026-08-02T18:21:10.599Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/873 carries the cohesive SDK/CLI intent-scoped read and universal output-contract delivery. Exact-head CI and review-loop evidence will remain on the PR to avoid appending unreviewed tracker mutations after bot approval."
  "2026-08-02T18:42:58.110Z","harness:codex","Correction to the 2026-08-02 live token-delta evidence: get:inspect increased from 2,851 to 2,946 estimated tokens, which is +95 tokens and approximately +3.3%, not -3.4%. The original append-only measurement remains preserved; this comment supersedes only its percentage label."
  "2026-08-02T19:34:16.143Z","harness:codex","Final review-correction evidence 2026-08-02: all 22 actionable CodeRabbit findings on PR #873 were implemented or resolved with explicit compatibility semantics. Runtime package authors now compose package intents; resolved command context reaches egress projection; canonical static encoding is distinct from legacy streaming behavior; narrowed SDK entrypoints expose executable read-contract primitives; and budgeted SDK reads return a discriminated omission type without widening ordinary calls. TypeScript, public-surface, contract, lint, docstring, duplication, token-budget, context/retrieval evaluation, fuzz, security, dependency-audit, and Sentry/telemetry gates pass. Final repository coverage is exact 100%: 47,849/47,849 statements, 34,528/34,528 branches, 9,777/9,777 functions, and 46,408/46,408 lines across 421 files and 6,735 tests. An unrelated packed install resolved only /tmp project node_modules and passed npm/npx plus Bun/bunx CLI and SDK execution at 2026.8.2."
  "2026-08-02T19:49:19.356Z","harness:codex","Exact-head CodeRabbit follow-up on PR #873: linked CHANGELOG.md through pm docs so the generated documentation change has owning-item evidence."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T17:54:29.381Z","harness:claude-code","Intent-split evidence measured 2026-07-25 on `pm next --json` (2,022-item workspace, default flags). Payload breakdown by top-level key, in bytes:\n\n- blocked: 5,450 (47% of the response)\n- decision_needed: 2,163 (19%)\n- ready: 2,116 (18%)\n- recommended: 660 (6%)\n- filters 214, summary 133, truncation 27\n\nThe agent asked one question — what should I work on next — and 66% of the answer describes work it explicitly cannot start. The recommendation itself, the actual answer, is 6%. This is the clearest single case for intent-scoped projection in the CLI: `next` today serves three distinct intents (pick my next task; show me what is stuck; show me what needs a human decision) in one unconditional payload, and an agent pays for all three every time.\n\nNote also that `--fields` is available on list (5 references in help), search (4), and get (3), but absent from `next` entirely and nearly absent from `context` (1). The two commands an agent runs first, and most often, are the two with the least projection control.\n\nSuggested intent names when this item defines the vocabulary, so the split follows the existing envelope rather than inventing new shapes: `--for next` (recommended only), `--for triage` (blocked + blockers), `--for decisions` (decision_needed). Companion buckets stay reachable, never removed — the pm-0z7n alias-preservation rule applies to output shape, not just spellings."
  "2026-07-30T09:22:13.264Z","harness:claude-code","Delivery landed 2026-07-30 via PR 822 and two of this item's own acceptance criteria are falsified by the shipped surface. Recording the derivation here because the two follow-on issues had to drop their discovered_from rows to avoid a reciprocal active cycle with this item.\n\nShipped: PM_CONTEXT_INTENT_CONTRACTS declares six command-and-intent pairs (context orient, context handoff, get inspect, list triage, next execute, search discover), each naming included_field_groups and a token_budget in contract data rather than code, and --for is rendered on the commands.\n\nFalsified AC, one canonical unknown-value error with a nearest-match suggestion: --for on context carries TWO validators with two exit codes and mutually exclusive advice. Owned by pm-ai45y9.\n\nFalsified AC, intent selection composes with the token budget without either overriding the other: the declared budget is written to an option key that three of the five commands do not accept, so it is silently discarded and the observed payload exceeds the declaration by up to 43.8x. Owned by pm-7hbfch.\n\nBoth are now blockers on this item. The remaining ACs (extensibility by workspace and package declaration, discoverability through contracts, published per-intent token delta evidence, byte-identical default when the intent is omitted) are untested by this session and stay open here."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T18:17:09.456Z","harness:codex",Context intent declarations must be request-scoped and composed before dispatch; a process-global registry makes concurrent workspaces nondeterministic. Preserve legacy byte output unless a canonical output control or intent explicitly opts into shaping.
